    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19a5319d_43520a0e",
        "filename": "include/trace/hooks/vendor_hooks.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1761165
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-15T00:44:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think so; the reason is the wmb() in tracepoint.c  Basically I thought that if the ordering of the write is guaranteed such that -\u003efunc is written last, there is an implicit rule here.  1) If it_func is null, we\u0027ll do nothing.  2) if it_func is non-null, (it_func_ptr)-\u003edata should already have been written.\n\nThis only works because we never delete anything.\n\nRegardless, your feedback is greatly appreciated.  Let me know if my logic above is incorrect.",
      "parentUuid": "9894d6c6_47f72c40",
      "revId": "9250bc57e31a340917f4bb5a88483370c38e2cfb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56a06b0b_f855393b",
        "filename": "include/trace/hooks/vendor_hooks.h",
