        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T16:00:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027ve guaranteed the write-side ordering, but if you don\u0027t have anything here, isn\u0027t it fair for the compiler to reorder the loads of -\u003efunc and -\u003edata? It might not, but it would be allowed. You need to somehow tell the compiler that -\u003edata must be loaded after -\u003efunc.",
      "parentUuid": "19a5319d_43520a0e",
      "revId": "9250bc57e31a340917f4bb5a88483370c38e2cfb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
